  xmlns:sercap="org.blockml.bml.compiler.serializer.capability"
  xmlns:serconfig="org.blockml.bml.compiler.serializer.config"
  xmlns:serdocumentation="org.blockml.bml.compiler.serializer.documentation"
  xmlns:seremit="org.blockml.bml.compiler.serializer.emit"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation">

  <name>LayerSeparation</name>
  <type>serdocumentation:LayerSeparation</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>Serializer vs parser vs BOM vs core</is>

  <documentation>Four layers relevant to serialization:

    org.blockml.bml.bom.* (@blockml/bom) — Urmodell data structures the serializer reads
    (BomDocument, BlockDefinition, MemberDefinition, SourceInfo, XmlTrivia, …).
    SerializeOptions and SerializeResult (B26) also live here.

    org.blockml.bml.compiler.serializer.* (this package) — emit rules (B12–B25), emit
    architecture, serialize() entry point contract.

    org.blockml.bml.definition.* (@blockml/core) — BML meta-model. V2 serializer reads
    Definition blocks + bml:xml for dynamic emit order. V1 uses a hardcoded snapshot.

    @blockml/parser — BML → BomDocument mapper (inverse direction). Does not own serializer rules.

    The serializer accepts any Urmodell provenance (parser or future BomBuilder.seal()).</documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="serdocumentation:ArchitectureOverview" relation="ReadNext"></see>
    <see type="bomdocumentation:LayerSeparation" relation="SeeAlso"></see>
  </references>

</block>
